  entry that stood under "NEEDS DECISION" is closed. It is no longer declared anywhere.

- `surt` 0.3.1 (AGPL-3.0) was replaced by `cytir/core/surtkey.py` (ADR-121; the `surt`
  entry that stood under "NEEDS DECISION" is closed). It is no longer declared in
  `pyproject.toml` or `requirements-ci.txt`. `tldextract` (BSD-3-Clause), which only
  `surt` required, left the dependency set with it.

### Test-only, not distributed

- `surt` 0.3.1 (AGPL-3.0) may be installed by a developer as a differential oracle for
  `tests/test_surtkey_oracle.py` for the transition period. It is not declared in any
  extra, not imported by shipped code, and the test skips when the package is absent.
  CI proves key parity from the sealed fixture `tests/fixtures/surtkey_parity.v1.jsonl`
  without it.

### Fetched model file: CharSplit n-gram table

- `ngram_probs.json` (40,447,815 bytes, sha256 `b145f5fba901698479d3e889255cf9342fe7e6c3593f80f7dc1932d1759be7bf`)
  from `dtuggener/CharSplit` at the same pinned commit, MIT, Copyright (c) Don Tuggener.
  A table of character n-gram probabilities (no text), trained on about 1M German nouns from
  Wikipedia (upstream README). Fetched by `python3 -m cytir.embed.fetch_models`, never vendored
  in this repository, refused on any sha256 mismatch. Basis and acceptance: Tim, ruling 26.

